    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493296708/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """Saturday October 26. 1901. I Tatti. Settignano.
The unutterable Gravina to lunch, with Emily, who is delightful. Bach in the afternoon, Stein to dinner, whose presence caused Janet and me to play innumerable games of Patience. 
Sunday October 27. 1901.
We walked to the Bagazzano with Horne, and then had a deadly tea with Miss Blood, about whom the worst bores in Florence tend to swarm. Began  Tom Sawyer  in the evening to liven us up. 
Monday October 28. 1901.
Music. B.B. paid several calls, and brought the Houghtons back to dinner. Lunched at Poggio with Lord Currie. 
Tuesday October 29. 1901.
Called on Mme. Turri at Villa Salviati, taking Mr. Ross who was gorgeous in a purple cloak. Zug, “G.B. Zug of Pitts, Pa.” came to dine """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 204 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1899-02> .

